   },
   {
    "en": "block DC from reaching the load"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "CE short-circuits RE for AC, so the signal does not develop negative feedback across RE and the gain stays high; RE still stabilises the DC."
  },
